# Files that a Linux container executes or parses must check out with LF
# endings regardless of the developer's platform. A shell script checked out
# with CRLF fails at exec — the shebang becomes "/bin/sh\r", which does not
# exist, and the error ("no such file or directory") names a path that plainly
# does exist, so it is a genuinely confusing failure.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
